# MNIST Digit Recognition

This project implements a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to classify handwritten digits using the MNIST dataset. The model is built and trained in Python using TensorFlow and Keras, and run on Google Colab.

##  Overview

- **Dataset**: [MNIST Handwritten Digits](http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/)
- **Model Type**: Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)
- **Tools**: TensorFlow, Keras, Google Colab
- **Accuracy**: Achieves ~98% accuracy on the test set

##  Model Architecture

- **Input Layer**: 28x28 grayscale image
- **Convolutional Layer**: 32 filters, 3x3 kernel, ReLU
- **Pooling Layer**: MaxPooling 2x2
- **Convolutional Layer**: 64 filters, 3x3 kernel, ReLU
- **Pooling Layer**: MaxPooling 2x2
- **Flatten + Dense Layers**
- **Output Layer**: 10 neurons with Softmax activation

##  How to Run

1. Open the notebook in [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/).
2. Run all cells step by step.
3. View training accuracy, test accuracy, and prediction results.

##  File Structure

- `MNIST_Digit_Recognition_Model_Using_CNN.ipynb`: Main implementation notebook

